        "original_id": "0d024b3e-a2ef-50d0-a728-2c5819326aa3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Dănilă Prepeleac\n- People: Ion Creangă\n- Topics: Romanian literature, folklore, fairy tales\n\nFacts:\n- Ion Creangă was born on March 1, 1837, and died on December 31, 1889.\n- Ion Creangă was a Moldavian, later Romanian writer, raconteur, and schoolteacher.\n- Ion Creangă was also known as Nică al lui Ștefan a Petrei, Ion Torcălău, and Ioan Ștefănescu.\n- Dănilă Prepeleac is an 1876 fantasy short story and fairy tale by Ion Creangă.\n- Dănilă Prepeleac has been translated occasionally as Danilo the Pole, Dănilă Haystack-Peg, or Danillo Nonsuch.\n- Dănilă Prepeleac has a theme that echoes influences from local folklore.",
